# What a child process wrote to a file, read back as words a message can
# quote (defect 337; design.md §4.17, §1.12). clang's error stream, the answer
# it gives to `-###`, and what a refused round's questions said all come back
# through a file under `build/`, and every reader of clang's words asks here.
#
# **One byte that is not UTF-8 dropped every word** until defect 337: the
# readers asked `read_file`, which refuses such a file whole, and each took the
# refusal for silence. clang prints a location's file name as the bytes it was
# given, measured on Apple clang 21 on this Mac with a header's `#line 1
# "caf<0xE9>.h"`: an author's extern disagreement became `internal error` at
# exit 2 over an empty line, a construction the layout check refuses built at
# exit 0, a tag the second round needed was never learned, and the header's
# warning was shown nowhere. Each such byte is now written by its value,
# `<0xE9>`, as `not_text.bytes_written` writes one (defect 241's reading of
# pkg-config's complaint, `cli/package_answer.hero`), so every marker and
# every other word survives it.
#
# Its own module because `cli/clang_floor.hero` reads clang's answer too, and
# `cli/toolchain.hero` imports that module: a reader there would be a cycle.

use module/reading
use not_text
use cli/strings

# What the child wrote at `path`: its own text where every byte is UTF-8, and
# where one is not, the text with each such byte written by its value
# (`not_text.faults_of` records every one of the first nine lines that hold
# any and the first of each line after, which is what a message quotes); a
# line ended `\r\n` read as one ended `\n`, as clang on Windows ends them
# (`toolchain.asked_of_clang` carries the measurement). A failure only where
# nothing could be read back: no file there, or one that would not read.
function words(path: str) -> str?
    read = reading.source_text(path)?
    return ok(strings.without_returns(not_text.bytes_written(read.text, faults: read.faults)))

## Tests

# Defect 337 at the read: a child's words holding a byte that is not UTF-8,
# committed as `pkg-config` gave them (defect 241's fixture), come back whole,
# the byte written by its value. `cli/toolchain.hero` holds the same of the
# words clang writes for a header whose `#line` names `caf<0xE9>.h`.
test "words a child wrote with a byte that is not UTF-8 are read back whole, the byte written by its value (defect 337)"
    said = words("tests/golden/surface-fixtures/notext241/complaint-latin1.txt").must()
    assert said == "Package caf<0xE9>x was not found in the pkg-config search path.\nPackage 'caf<0xE9>x', required by 'u3', not found\n"

    # Text is itself, a return before a line end is no part of a line, and a
    # file that is not there is no answer anybody gave.
    assert !write_file(path: "build/selftest-read-back.txt", text: "one\r\ntwo\n").is_err()
    assert words("build/selftest-read-back.txt").must() == "one\ntwo\n"
    assert words("build/selftest-read-back-none.txt").is_err()
